{"type":"text","timestamp":1794522683712,"sessionID":"ses_e2e209c6fffekjqz9ELii6MPkV","part":{"id":"prt_1d1e30a47002g85upvi8MUyTbk","sessionID":"ses_e2e209c6fffekjqz9ELii6MPkV","messageID":"msg_1d1e2f3b1001Cld5RWrYYCpoDg","type":"text","text":"T017 is implemented and the verify command prints `fresh`.\n\n**File written**\n\n`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`\n\n`doctorLeadPhrases` now derives the route policy with `derivePolicy` and rejects any lead phrase that carries no state or health word unless that policy is `ask`. I added `LEAD_PHRASE_STATE_WORDS` and a `hasStateWord` helper that matches whole words, so `on` inside `environment` cannot clear a phrase. The existing `disable comment hygiene gate` phrase survives because its `/doctor:git hooks` route is `mutates` and therefore derives `ask`.\n\n**Verify output**\n\nCommand: `node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs --check`\n\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"fresh\",\n  \"counts\": {\n    \"commandMetadata\": 23,\n    \"allowList\": 4,\n    \"doctorRoutes\": 35,\n    \"generated\": 62,\n    \"typescriptActive\": 45,\n    \"pythonActive\": 51\n  },\n  \"changed\": []\n}\n```\n\nExit status 0. Baseline before the edit was the same `fresh`, so the generated files are unchanged.\n\nBecause `--check` alone cannot show the rejection firing, I exercised the shipped function in isolation through a temporary in-memory module load. It returned `rejected -> ... needs a state or health word` for a `read-only` route with `disable the gate`, `accepted` for the same phrase on a `mutates` doctor route, and `accepted` for `which gate is off` on a `read-only` route.\n\n**Notes**\n\nI did not tick the T017 checkbox in `tasks.md`. No other file was edited, and the other modified paths in `git status` belong to other workers. One residual detail: for a standalone command with per-action risk keys, the policy is derived from the item's own keys, not each action's. The only current standalone lead phrase contains `check`, so it passes under either reading.","time":{"start":1794522679879,"end":1794522683712}}}
